// java/hello_world's wire type -- byte-identical to zig/hello_world,
// c/hello_world, and cpp/hello_world's idl/hello_world.idl. See
// docs/design/hello-world-reference-app.md at the repo root for the full
// spec. Deliberately keyless: per DDS 1.4 2.2.2.1, "If no key is provided,
// the data set associated with the Topic is restricted to a single
// instance" -- a keyless Topic is fully spec-legitimate, and zidl's
// --generate-zzdds-wrappers (Java backend) generates
// TypeSupport/DataWriter/DataReader for it (see
// zidl/src/backend/java.zig's isZzddsTopicStructJava and
// emitStructSerializeFns' --generate-zzdds-wrappers branch).
//
// Note: the generated outer wrapper class is named from this file's stem
// ("Hello_world"), not from the struct name -- HelloWorld itself (and its
// DataWriter/DataReader/TypeSupport) are named directly from the struct,
// so there's no collision; see java/hello_world/README.md.
@appendable
struct HelloWorld {
    int32 count;
    string<256> message;
};
